Add GDMS end-of-day channel assignment (v0.117)

Replaces the manual end-of-day process of working out what shipped to
GDMS-enabled customers and assigning those devices' MACs to the right
GDMS channel by hand.

Backend:
- V51 migration: Company.gdmsChannelId/gdmsChannelName (which GDMS
  channel a company's despatched devices go to) and
  StockItem.gdmsSyncedAt (idempotency - a device is only ever assigned
  to GDMS once).
- GdmsSignatureUtil: GDMS's per-request HMAC-style signature algorithm
  (materially different from DPD's plain bearer token - see
  gdms-api-findings.md for the full write-up).
- GdmsAuthService: OAuth password-grant token caching, mirroring
  DpdAuthService's credentials-fingerprint pattern.
- GdmsChannelService: live /sub/list channel lookup with a
  Settings-cached fallback (same shape as DpdShippingService's Service
  dropdown), and assignMacsToChannel() batching MACs in groups of 100
  - a prior manual process reportedly hit a 500-unit limit, so this
  stays well under that and keeps one failing batch from losing an
  entire day's despatch.
- GdmsEndOfDayService: reads "despatched today" from StockMovement
  (type DESPATCH, one row per item with its own accurate createdAt)
  rather than Order.despatchedAt, which is set once and never updated
  on a re-opened/multi-shipment order. Groups despatched,
  not-yet-synced items by company, skips anything not GDMS-enabled or
  without a channel set, and assigns each company's devices via
  GdmsChannelService.
- Three triggers: a 16:30 scheduled job, a global "run now" button
  (Settings > GDMS), and a per-order button (Sales Activity) scoped to
  just that order's despatched-but-unsynced items.

Frontend:
- Settings > GDMS: credentials (region, client ID/secret,
  username/password), Reset GDMS connection, and Run GDMS end-of-day
  now with a result summary.
- Companies: GDMS channel dropdown (live/cached, mirrors the DPD
  Service dropdown UX), shown once GDMS is ticked for a company.
- Sales Activity/OrderEdit: "Assign despatched devices to GDMS"
  button, shown only for a GDMS-enabled customer with a channel set.

gdms-api-findings.md updated with the final implementation decisions
(base URL, batch size, idempotency approach).

